# Excom — Omnichannel Communication Platform

Frappe app consolidating WhatsApp, Email, Instagram into a unified real-time inbox, integrated with ERPNext.

## Stack
- Backend: Python 3.10+, Frappe Framework, ERPNext
- Frontend: React + Tailwind CSS (custom pages), Frappe UI (standard)
- Database: MariaDB via Frappe ORM
- Realtime: Frappe Socket.IO
- APIs: Gmail API (OAuth2), WhatsApp Business API, Instagram Graph API

## Commands
- `bench start` — dev server
- `bench build --app excom` — build frontend
- `bench run-tests --app excom` — all tests
- `bench run-tests --app excom --module excom.tests.test_<name>` — single module
- `bench migrate` — apply schema changes
- `bench console` — Python REPL with Frappe context

## Key Architecture
- **Omni Identity**: links contacts across channels to ERPNext Customer/Lead
- **Assignment Engine**: routes conversations via territory rules or round-robin
- **Pointer-based Email**: stores Gmail message IDs, not full bodies
- **Channel Adapter Pattern**: common interface per channel

## Directory
```
excom/excom/
├── communication/    # Core doctypes (Conversation, Message)
├── channel/          # WhatsApp, Email, Instagram integrations
├── crm/              # CRM connectivity, Omni Identity
├── assignment/       # Assignment Engine
├── api/              # REST endpoints
├── public/js/        # React frontend app
└── tests/            # Test modules
```
